A worker receives a bounded projection of the knowledge system at boot, queries deeper evidence through its tool profile only when the task needs it, and never writes knowledge. Its feedback reaches the store after the run closes, through the summarizer job and the librarian. Code: worker/context.ts assembles the boot context; profiles/defaults.ts names the tools.

## Boot Context

The rendered context is three blocks in order: the packet context, the legacy graph file card, and the V2 target card. The last two appear only when their data exists.

| Block | Contents | Source |
| --- | --- | --- |
| context_budget | The budget mode and the inline source limit | Chosen by the worker cycle; degrades across retries |
| Worker packet | Repair request when one exists, the target with its source inlined at the budget's limit, baseline evidence, the available-tools listing, canonical tool paths, decomp standards | The claimed target packet and the standards files |
| Graph file card | Structural neighbors from the legacy code graph | code_graph_file_card over the legacy code graph store (kept) |
| Target card | Ledger (integration outcomes on runs: a conflicted run lists up to 10 conflict paths), facts by type, links, from V2 records | card.ts, gated on data presence |

**Context budgets**

| Budget | Inline source limit | Tools | Standards | Graph card | Target card |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| full | 32,000 chars | Full tool XML | Every accepted, worker-facing standard | Full | 20 ledger entries, 8 links, 3 facts per link |
| compact | 12,000 chars | Tool names only | Five-rule condensation | Compacted | 8 entries, 4 links, 1 fact per link |
| minimal | 3,000 chars | Tool names only | Two-rule condensation | Minimal | 3 entries, 2 links, no facts per link |

Target Card has the card shape and its gates. The graph file card is rendered by code_graph_file_card over the legacy code graph under apps/server/src/core/knowledge/graph, a kept legacy surface outside the V2 store..

`renamed_from` and the drift report are librarian-context fields, carried by the `pr_imported` and `run_closed` contexts, not worker-card fields: the worker sees a rename only as the target it was handed, and drift only through the facts the librarian re-cited — see Drift Gate.

## Tools

Eleven of the worker's 31 tools read knowledge. The six kv2_* tools read the V2 store directly, read-only; the four graph tools read the legacy code graph, which is kept outside the V2 store; past_prs_search reads the past-PRs archive. The V2 target card still arrives pre-rendered at boot. ledger_search was retired on 2026-09-03.

| Tool | Reads | Status |
| --- | --- | --- |
| code_graph_file_card | The legacy code graph: files, units, functions, match state, one-hop edges | Legacy graph store, kept |
| code_graph_search | Legacy graph search chunks | Legacy graph store, kept |
| knowledge_graph_search | Legacy graph learning projections | Legacy graph store, kept |
| graph_related_functions | Callers, callees, opseq analogs from the legacy graph | Legacy graph store, kept |
| past_prs_search | The past-PRs archive | Live |
| kv2_subject_record | The assembled V2 record for another target or entity | Live, V2 store |
| kv2_pr_search | Archived pull request summaries and discussion | Live, V2 store |
| kv2_discord_search | Archived Discord messages by text, channel, author, or time range | Live, V2 store |
| kv2_wiki_search | The latest mirrored wiki revision | Live, V2 store |
| kv2_attempt_search | Structured prior worker attempts, narrowed by hypothesis text | Live, V2 store |
| kv2_resolve_locator | The exact source material behind a Discord, wiki, PR, attempt, or code locator | Live, V2 store |

## Ship Gate

Standards are enforced, not consulted, at the gate. The deterministic layer is the review_lint diff scan: every finding cites the standard it violates, the scan fails closed when the scanner cannot run, and the QA verdict is combined into the handoff verdict. The worker-side check and the regression-check gate both go through the same scanner. Code: scan-diff.ts, qa-gate.ts.

<!-- sequence: ./assets/sequences/worker-knowledge-loop.sequence.json title="Worker boot, ship gate, and the feedback path" -->

## Feedback

The worker leaves no knowledge behind by itself. What it did becomes knowledge in three steps after the run closes.

```process-outline
The runner closes the worker state; with --worker-summary on, a worker_summary job is enqueued for it (default off; a catch-up pass enqueues any closed state that lacks one)
The summarizer turns the transcript and checkpoint digest into a worker_run, its submissions, and a run_narrative, then enqueues a run_closed index task
The librarian consumes the task and decides, per touched target and entity, whether any fact changes; the apply layer writes
```

## Related

- Worker: the agent page: context inputs, tools, when it runs.

- Standards: what the gate enforces.

- Run Closed: the pathway the feedback takes.


